{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>For like the sound of the sirim.</b> Like thorns, from the language of 'הנני סך את דרכך בסירי' (I am blocking your path with thorns). The meaning is that He places sirim and thorns on their path. And 'under the pot' is like 'בשבתנו על סיר הבשר' (when we sat by the pot of meat). 'סיר' (pot) and 'סירים' (thorns) come together though they are not from one meaning; it is a figure of speech, like 'רוכבים על שלשים עירים' (riding on thirty donkeys) and 'שלשים עירים להם' (thirty cities they have). He said 'this too is vanity,' reverting to the song of fools: their laughter and joy have no substance; the meaning is that it is only a sound and outcry, like the sound of thorns."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The Hebrew cites Judges 5:10 (עירים = donkeys, homonymous with ערים = cities in v.11); both puns are left in Hebrew. The verse reference for 'הנני סך את דרכך בסירים' is Ezekiel 3:20, not resolved explicitly by Ibn Ezra."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:28:04.950522906Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}